WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.460
- So, okay.

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:04.430
What are you teaching me today?

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:08.352
- Eggs with chickpeas and tomato sauce.

00:00:08.352 --> 00:00:09.930
You can do it in five minutes.

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:13.070
- I mean, that's revelatory
because that's such a deterrent

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:15.800
because when they say
prep time 20 minutes,

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.710
cook time 60 minutes,

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:21.050
it's not realistic for
a lot of people's lives.

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:22.350
- So listen, we have the pan.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.940
We have the oil, and you have garlic?

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:27.744
- I have garlic right here.

00:00:27.744 --> 00:00:31.470
- Put the garlic on the pan,
and now talk to your garlic.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:32.510
Tell, "Hey garlic, how are you?

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:34.350
How are you doing, baby?"

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:36.560
- Hey, baby, how's it going?

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:38.970
My kids' grandfather, Arie,
that's what he always says.

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:40.433
Hey, baby.

00:00:40.433 --> 00:00:42.300
- The garlic is speaking back to you,

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.907
and the garlic is telling you,

00:00:44.907 --> 00:00:48.630
"Oh, I'm so happy I'm
cooking with Drew and Jose.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:49.870
It's amazing."

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:51.270
- I love garlic.

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:52.988
The more, the better.

00:00:52.988 --> 00:00:55.870
- Okay, so in this moment,
we put the chickpeas now.

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:56.703
- Roger that.

00:00:56.703 --> 00:01:00.980
- This is actually great
to buy a can of chickpeas,

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:02.060
which are delicious,

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:05.140
and usually they have very
good price on the supermarket.

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:06.050
- I was going to say,

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:10.440
I think they're a very
healthy thing for people,

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:13.880
and you have a vegetable
book, and for vegetarians

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:17.330
that are really satisfying
protein substitute.

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:18.510
I love them.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:20.440
- So you take a look at the chickpeas.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:23.610
They're so happy because they
love to be with the garlic.

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:26.580
People don't know this
but chickpeas and garlic,

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:28.260
they're very friendly, okay?

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:30.610
You have to lift up the temperature.

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:32.060
Put higher temperature, Drew.

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:34.650
- Oh, Jose, I'm so excited to tell you

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:36.050
that I just did that.

00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:38.530
That means we're
telepathically linked now.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:39.980
I'm in.

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:42.652
- So in this moment,
this is very important.

00:01:42.652 --> 00:01:45.300
I will add a little bit
more of oil to your pan.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.990
I love olive oil.

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:49.967
- By the way, check this olive oil out.

00:01:49.967 --> 00:01:51.640
Oh, hang on, beauty shot.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:52.560
There we go.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:53.900
I love your olive oil.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.500
Thank you so much for sending it to us.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:58.340
- Let's say you have fresh tomatoes.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:02.740
You can get a peeled fresh
tomato and cut it in cubes,

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:07.740
or you have canned tomatoes,
and also works very well,

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:14.680
or you have any pasta tomato
sauce that is already made.

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:18.128
Everything works.

00:02:18.128 --> 00:02:19.900
Just make sure that you
do whatever you have

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:21.340
at home is what you use.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:24.430
- I think that makes people
less stressed in the kitchen.

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:25.940
Thank you.

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:29.710
- Drew, recipes should
be like life itself.

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:33.620
When you don't have
some of the ingredients,

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:37.520
just move on, change the
recipe in your dishes

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:40.240
or in your life, and you'll
always be successful.

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:42.880
That's a very important lesson in cooking.

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:43.822
- And in life.

00:02:43.822 --> 00:02:46.770
(audience applauding)

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:50.470
Jose, look, I'm sizzling, baby!

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:54.813
- So now, I have a can
of Spanish pimenton,

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:57.300
what we call paprika.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:58.420
If you have it.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:01.310
If you don't have
paprika, put chili flakes.

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:03.650
If you don't have, put cumin.

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:07.800
If you don't, put whatever
spice you have in your kitchen.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.840
Make the recipe your own.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:13.320
- Oh, paprika, I love you so.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:15.730
- And now, I'm putting the tomato in.

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:18.700
Because this tomato is already cooked,

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:20.040
it's going to be easy.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.330
I mean, I cannot believe, Drew,

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:24.573
that I am actually cooking with you.

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:28.897
I mean, when I told my
daughters, they were like,

00:03:28.897 --> 00:03:29.930
"Come on, daddy.

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:30.971
Don't make fun of us."

00:03:30.971 --> 00:03:32.371
Okay, I'm cooking.

00:03:32.371 --> 00:03:33.690
I'm cooking with Drew Barrymore.

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:35.280
I'm cooking with her.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:37.100
- Jose, how old are your daughters?

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:38.630
- I have three.

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:43.630
Carlota, she's 21, Ines,
she's 19, and Lucia, she's 16.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:46.300
So listen, this is very important.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:50.550
Now this tomato sauce, the
chickpea, everything is cooked,

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:54.370
and I am putting inside four or five eggs.

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:57.550
In this moment, you put
some salt on the eggs,

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:00.753
and ladies and gentleman,
to cover the pot,

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:04.700
and now you can open a glass of wine.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:06.640
You're gonna open yourself a beer.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:09.000
You can drink a sherry.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.910
So why I'm doing this one pot, Drew,

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:14.040
because very often, many recipes,

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:16.850
they require three or four or five pots.

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:18.430
You can make everything with one pot.

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:19.600
No cleaning.

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:20.433
This is great.

00:04:20.433 --> 00:04:21.690
- I love one pot.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:26.690
I think it really helps people
feel like they can manage.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:30.447
If they're not, I'm just
not that girl, who's like,

00:04:30.447 --> 00:04:33.020
"So Betty, how was your day?"

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:34.620
I'm just stirring and casual.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:35.506
I'm like.

00:04:35.506 --> 00:04:38.500
(Drew screaming)

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:43.500
So one pot for me is a great
way to cook that keeps me calm.

00:04:44.809 --> 00:04:47.420
- This pandemic I've been
cooking a lot with my daughters,

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:51.290
and we did some cooking on social media.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:54.230
And quite frankly, we were
doing it because it was fun,

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:56.110
because we were spending so many hours,

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:58.280
and we began sharing it with people.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:01.040
And was one of the best
moments of my life,

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:03.080
to be cooking with my three daughters.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:06.850
Already, man, I remember
that first time I had them

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:08.397
in my arms and I was crying.

00:05:08.397 --> 00:05:10.730
It was after they came up into the world,

00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:14.120
and now 21 years later, I
realize through this pandemic

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:16.710
that they are these three grown up girls.

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:18.120
And to me, cooking with my daughters

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:20.470
has been the happiest moment of my life.

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:23.433
- Look at that, look at that, beauty shot!

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:29.163
And now I'm going to try it.

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:31.823
- Okay.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:35.990
- Yup, oh yeah.

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:37.640
Oh God, that's good.

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:40.270
- The great thing about this dish is that

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:42.200
you can make it your own in so many ways.

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:43.640
You can cook it every time,

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:45.170
and every time be a different recipe.

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:46.700
You can put some mozzarella.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:48.445
You can put some manchego cheese.

00:05:48.445 --> 00:05:53.445
- Ooh, topping it with
cheese would kick it up

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:55.720
a whole other level, you're right.

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:59.010
- And don't be afraid
of trying new things.

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:01.580
Always, you take risk.

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:03.163
They will always pay off.

00:06:03.163 --> 00:06:06.163
(audience cheering)

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:12.230
- Jose, you make the world a better place

00:06:12.230 --> 00:06:15.601
and you help us be better
people with your wisdom.

00:06:15.601 --> 00:06:18.184
(upbeat music)

